 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Pronombres after preposition",
   "texto": [
    "After many prepositions, tonic forms are used: **para mim** (for me), **para ti** (for you), **para ele/ela** (for him / her).",
    "With **com**, some forms are written in one word: **comigo** (with me), **contigo** (with you). Learn these forms within short expressions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Pronombres with the infinitive",
   "texto": [
    "With **vou**, **quero**, **posso** or **vais**, the pronoun goes **detrás** of the infinitive: **vou visitá-lo** (I will visit it), **quero comprá-la** (I want to buy it).",
    "When the infinitive ends in **-r**, the form is: **visitar** → **visitá-lo**, **comprar** → **comprá-la**, **fazer** → **fazê-lo**, **ver** → **vê-los**."
   ]
  },
